  "id": "COMPOUND:757 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which etoposide may interact with Phosphodiesterase 6C, through a series of molecular interactions involving palmarumycin CP18. Etoposide is known to target ubiquitin carboxyl-terminal hydrolase 5 and P2X purinoceptor 7, both of which are inhibited by palmarumycin CP18. This inhibition leads to the subsequent targeting of Phosphodiesterase 6C, indicating a possible pathway where etoposide indirectly influences the activity of Phosphodiesterase 6C via palmarumycin CP18. The shared involvement of palmarumycin CP18 in multiple pathways highlights a potential common mechanism, though the exact role of etoposide in this process remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between etoposide and Phosphodiesterase 6C, but further experimental validation is required to confirm the direct interaction and the precise biological consequences.",
